        "5"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 2,
      "answerSource": "derived",
      "answerKeyRef": null,
      "explanation": "Single-shear value of one 16 mm shop rivet at 100 MPa = (pi/4)(16^2)(100) = 20.1 kN, which is less than bearing on the 6 mm plate (16 x 6 x 300 = 28.8 kN), so shear governs. Number of rivets = 80/20.1 = 3.98, rounded up to 4. The stress values are assumed from standard steel-design practice, not stated on the page.",
